    "# RS-DAT: start here\n",
    "\n",
{% if api %}
    "This workspace runs **JupyterLab** with **Dask on Snellius** and a **Prefect** server. Work through this notebook once to connect it to Snellius; after that you only repeat step 1 when your Slurm token expires.\n",
{% else %}
    "This workspace runs **JupyterLab** with **Dask on Snellius** and a **Prefect** server. Work through this notebook once to connect it to Snellius.\n",
{% endif %}
    "\n",
    "**How it works**\n",
    "\n",
{% if ws %}
    "- **JupyterLab** and the **Dask scheduler** run here, on this Research Cloud workspace.\n",
{% else %}
    "- **JupyterLab** runs here, on this Research Cloud workspace. The **Dask scheduler** runs as a Slurm job on Snellius, next to the workers, and this notebook reaches it through an SSH tunnel that the job opens back to this workspace.\n",
{% endif %}
{% if api %}
    "- **Dask workers** run as Slurm jobs on Snellius. The workspace submits and cancels them through the **Slurm REST API**, with your **Slurm token**{{ '' if sshuttle else ': no SSH login to Snellius from here' }}.\n",
{% else %}
    "- **Dask workers** run as Slurm jobs on Snellius. The workspace submits and cancels them over **SSH** on the login node `{{ rsdat_slurm_host }}`, with an SSH key of this workspace that you register once.\n",
{% endif %}
{% if gw %}
    "- The workers connect to the scheduler here. For the other direction, a small **gateway job** on Snellius opens an SSH tunnel back to this workspace. It starts with your first cluster and stops when the last one closes.\n",
{% elif sshuttle %}
    "- The workers connect to the scheduler here. For the other direction, **sshuttle** routes the workers' network through one SSH connection from this workspace to the login node `{{ rsdat_slurm_host }}`, with the same key.\n",
{% elif ws %}
    "- The workers connect to the scheduler here, and the scheduler connects to them directly.\n",
{% endif %}
    "- **Prefect** runs here too, at `/prefect/` next to `/jupyter/`. Flows can run their tasks on the Dask workers.\n",
    "- All Dask traffic is encrypted with this workspace's own certificate.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is your copy: edit it freely. The original is in `/opt/rsdat/share/RS-DAT-start-here.ipynb`."
   ],
   "id": "rsdat-00"
  },
{% if api %}
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1{{ 'a' if ssh_key else '' }}. Your Slurm token\n",
    "\n",
    "The workspace acts on Snellius with a token that you create there.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Log in to Snellius (SSH, with your second factor) and run, for a token valid for one day:\n",
    "\n",
    "   ```\n",
    "   scontrol token lifespan=86400\n",
    "   ```\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Copy the line it prints (`SLURM_JWT=eyJ...`).\n",
    "3. Run the next cell and paste it. It's stored in `~/.config/rsdat/slurm.env`, readable only by this workspace's JupyterLab user.\n",
    "\n",
    "In a terminal, `rsdat-slurm-token` does the same, and `rsdat-slurm-token --status` shows when the token expires. New terminals show it too."
   ],
   "id": "rsdat-01"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import getpass, subprocess\n",
    "\n",
    "token = getpass.getpass(\"Slurm token (the SLURM_JWT=... line): \")\n",
    "result = subprocess.run([\"rsdat-slurm-token\"], input=token + \"\\n\", text=True, capture_output=True)\n",
    "print(result.stdout or result.stderr)\n",
    "del token"
   ],
   "id": "rsdat-02"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Check that Snellius answers with your token (lists your jobs, probably none yet):"
