   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. A Dask cluster on Snellius\n",
    "\n",
    "`RSDATSLURMCluster` takes its defaults (partition, cores, memory, walltime, worker image) from `/etc/dask/rsdat.yaml`; override them per cluster, e.g. `RSDATSLURMCluster(cores=8, memory=\"16GiB\", walltime=\"02:00:00\")`.\n",
    "\n",
{% if gw %}
    "Creating the first cluster submits the gateway job and waits for it, so it takes as long as that job waits in the queue. `scale` then submits worker jobs, which join when they start.\n",
    "\n",
{% if rsdat_dask_gateway_worker | bool %}
    "- The gateway job also runs a worker, `rsdat-gateway-1` ({{ rsdat_dask_gateway_worker_cores }} threads: the job has {{ rsdat_dask_gateway_cores }} cores, on Snellius the share it charges for anyway, and keeps the rest for the tunnel). So `scale(jobs=2)` gives three workers. Before the gateway job reaches its walltime ({{ rsdat_dask_gateway_walltime }}) a new one takes over without a gap; its worker is `rsdat-gateway-2`, and so on.\n",
{% endif %}
{% elif not ws %}
    "Creating a cluster submits the scheduler job and waits for it, so it takes as long as that job waits in the queue. `scale` then submits worker jobs, which join when they start.\n",
    "\n",
{% else %}
    "`scale` submits worker jobs, which join when they start.\n",
    "\n",
{% endif %}
{% if ws %}
    "- One cluster at a time per workspace: the scheduler always listens on port {{ rsdat_dask_scheduler_port }}. Close a cluster (in the sidebar or a notebook) before creating the next.\n",
    "\n",
{% endif %}
    "The **Dask** sidebar on the left does the same: **New** creates a cluster, **Scale** adds workers, and its dashboard links open through JupyterLab."
   ],
   "id": "rsdat-05"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from rsdat_dask import RSDATSLURMCluster\n",
    "from distributed import Client\n",
    "\n",
    "cluster = RSDATSLURMCluster()\n",
    "cluster.scale(jobs=2)\n",
    "client = Client(cluster)\n",
    "client.wait_for_workers(2, timeout=900)\n",
    "client"
   ],
   "id": "rsdat-06"
  },
  {
