    "## 3. Prefect\n",
    "\n",
    "The Prefect UI is at **`/prefect/`** on this workspace (the Access menu of the workspace, or replace `/jupyter/...` by `/prefect/` in the address bar). It uses the same SRAM login as JupyterLab, so it doesn't ask for a password. (Notebooks and the Dask workers use the machine API at `/prefect/machine-api/` with Prefect's own password, already set in `PREFECT_API_URL` and `PREFECT_API_AUTH_STRING`.)\n",
    "\n",
    "Flows run from notebooks report to that server. With `DaskTaskRunner`, their tasks run on the Dask workers on Snellius:"
   ],
   "id": "rsdat-11"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from prefect import flow, task\n",
    "from prefect_dask import DaskTaskRunner\n",
    "\n",
    "cluster = RSDATSLURMCluster()\n",
    "cluster.scale(jobs=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "@task\n",
    "def where(x):\n",
    "    import socket\n",
    "    return x, socket.gethostname()\n",
    "\n",
    "@flow(log_prints=True, task_runner=DaskTaskRunner(address=cluster.scheduler_address))\n",
    "def hello_snellius(n: int = 4):\n",
    "    for x, host in [f.result() for f in where.map(range(n))]:\n",
    "        print(x, \"ran on\", host)\n",
    "\n",
    "hello_snellius()\n",
    "cluster.close()"
   ],
   "id": "rsdat-12"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## When something doesn't work\n",
    "\n",
    "| What you see | Likely cause | What to do |\n",
    "| --- | --- | --- |\n",
{% if api %}
    "| `sbatch`/`squeue` errors about authentication | No token, or it expired | Step 1 again; `rsdat-slurm-token --status` |\n",
{% else %}
    "| `Permission denied (publickey)` from `sbatch`/`squeue` | The SSH key isn't registered (yet) | Step 1: add the key in the CUA portal, wait a few minutes; test with `ssh -F /etc/rsdat/slurm-ssh.conf rsdat-slurm true` |\n",
{% endif %}
{% if ws %}
    "| `Address already in use` (port {{ rsdat_dask_scheduler_port }}) | Another cluster is still running, in the sidebar or another notebook | Close it, or restart that notebook's kernel |\n",
{% endif %}
    "| An error saying Slurm refused the job | Partition, account, cores, memory or walltime not accepted | The settings named in the error (`/etc/dask/rsdat.yaml`, or arguments to `RSDATSLURMCluster`) |\n",
{% if gw and api %}
    "| Creating a cluster takes long | The gateway job waits in the queue | `squeue --user \"$(rsdat-slurm-token --user)\"` shows its state |\n",
{% elif gw %}
    "| Creating a cluster takes long | The gateway job waits in the queue | `squeue --me` shows its state |\n",
{% elif not ws %}
    "| Creating a cluster takes long | The scheduler job waits in the queue | `squeue --me` shows its state |\n",
{% endif %}
    "| Workers never join | They can't reach the scheduler, or the job failed | The job logs on Snellius, in `~/.rsdat/dask-logs/` |\n",
{% if gw %}
    "| Results don't come back | The gateway job stopped | `dask-gateway-<job id>.log` in the same directory |\n",
{% elif sshuttle %}
    "| Results don't come back | sshuttle isn't connected | `systemctl status rsdat-sshuttle` (the key must be registered; the login node needs `python3`) |\n",
{% endif %}
    "| Errors about versions or unpickling | Worker environment differs from this workspace | `client.get_versions(check=True)` |\n",
    "\n",
    "Each Dask job writes its log on Snellius in `~/.rsdat/dask-logs/` ({{ '`dask-gateway-<id>.log`, ' if gw else ('`dask-scheduler-<id>.log`, ' if not ws else '') }}`dask-worker-<id>.log`)."
   ],
